0,Lolopo language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lolopo_language,"Chinese speakers call it Central Yi, as the name Lolopo does not exist in Chinese. It is one of the six Yi languages recognized by the government of China. The Lolo language is mainly spoken in central Yunnan. It is also spoken in Laos. In Laos, Lolo is spoken in three villages of Phongsaly Province. An alternative spelling of Lolopo is Lolopho.","Lolopo, Southern",Sino-Tibetan
1,Southern Lolopo language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/?title=Southern_Lolopo_language&redirect=no,Appearance Redirect to: Lolopo language Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 License,"Lolopo, Southern",Sino-Tibetan
2,Music of Tibet - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Tibet,"May 6, 2026 - The music of Tibet reflects the cultural heritage of the trans-Himalayan region centered in Tibet, but also known wherever Indigenous Tibetan groups are found in Nepal, Bhutan, India and further abroad. The religious music of Tibet reflects the profound influence of Tibetan Buddhism on the culture.","Lolopo, Southern",Sino-Tibetan
3,Lolopo language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_639:ysp,"March 28, 2025 - Tu 土 (Tuzu 土族): lo21 lo33 ... in southern Xiangyun County) Qiangyi 羌夷: lɔ̠21 lɔ33 sɨ55 (spoken by nearly 15,000 people in northern and central Xiangyun County) Eastern Lalu: lo̠21 lo̠33 (spoken by nearly 20,000 people in Xinping County and Zhenyuan County). The Xinping dialect is documented in Wang (2020). In Xinping County, there are about 3,000 ethnic ""Lalu"" (腊鲁; i.e., Lolopo) in Malutang ...","Lolopo, Southern",Sino-Tibetan
4,Loloish languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loloish,"May 23, 2026 - However, per Bradley and Thurgood there is also a central branch, with languages from both northern and southern. Bradley adds a fourth, southeastern branch. Northern Loloish: Nuosu (2 million), Nasu (1.0 million), etc. Central Loloish: Lisu (940,000)–Lipho (250,000) (incl. Lolopo (570,000), ...","Lolopo, Southern",Sino-Tibetan
5,Sino-Tibetan languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sino-Tibetan_languages,"June 3, 2026 - Most of the current spread of Sino-Tibetan languages is the result of historical expansions of the three groups with the most speakers – Chinese, Burmese and Tibetic – replacing an unknown number of earlier languages. These groups also have the longest literary traditions of the family. The remaining languages are spoken in mountainous areas, along the southern ...","Lolopo, Southern",Sino-Tibetan
6,"Lolopo, Southern Language (YSP) – L1 & L2 Speakers, Status ...",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/ysp/,"Southern Lolopo is an endangered indigenous language of China. It belongs to the Sino-Tibetan language family. The language is used as a first language by all adults in the ethnic community, but not all young people. It is not known to be taught in schools.","Lolopo, Southern",Sino-Tibetan
7,Lolopo Yi Music in Yunnan (1) | Lolopo Artists in Yunnan | XY,https://xy3mas93.bandcamp.com/album/lolopo-yi-music-in-yunnan-1,"Dec 14, 2025 · Lolopo, or so called Central Yi, is a major subgroup under Yi ethnic in China. They share a similarity with Lisu, and are famous for their Sixian arts including Left Feet Dance and Me Ge.","Lolopo, Southern",Sino-Tibetan
